description:
Found by zenajco-lib-split (2026-09-15). String + concat under --dce produces a module wasm-tools validate rejects with 'unknown function 127: function index out of bounds' — index-space desync, same family as the zena:math div DCE bug (function indices baked before DCE removes/import-shifts something). Bisected minimal repro (A invalid, B valid):

A (invalid):
  import { String } from 'zena:string';
  import { writeLine } from 'lib/zena/wasip2/stdout.zena';
  export let run = (): void => { writeLine('a' + 'b'); };

B (valid): same imports + clocks/random/Memory touched, no concat anywhere.

Build: node ~/src/zena-jco-fork/packages/cli/lib/cli.js build A.zena --dce -o a.wasm; wasm-tools validate a.wasm -> error. Scratch pair at .test-agent/libsplit/ (gitignored — repro embedded here). Lib/example code currently avoids concat (documented hazard in lib/zena/README.md).
